Depth-First Search (DFS) Cycle Detection in Directed Graphs in Python

Using 3-color marking (White = unvisited, Gray = visiting/in call stack, Black = completed).
If a DFS encounters a Gray node, a cycle exists!

Python Code:
```python
def has_cycle(num_nodes: int, edges: list[tuple]) -> bool:
    adj = {i: [] for i in range(num_nodes)}
    for u, v in edges: adj[u].append(v)

    visited = [0] * num_nodes # 0: unvisited, 1: visiting, 2: visited

    def dfs(u):
        visited[u] = 1
        for v in adj[u]:
            if visited[v] == 1: return True # Cycle found
            if visited[v] == 0 and dfs(v): return True
        visited[u] = 2
        return False

    return any(dfs(i) for i in range(num_nodes) if visited[i] == 0)
```
